ServiceNow Agent — Deliverables
Create the ticket/interaction creation workflow function — HTTP-triggered Azure Function as the orchestrator's single entry point.
Implement action-routing logic for the full ticket lifecycle — create interaction, create incident, update incident, resolve, close.
Implement ticket-to-incident conversion for unresolved cases — an open interaction is escalated into an incident under the same conversation.
Create a common, reusable agent-integration framework — Foundry Responses API + agent_reference, ready to reuse for future API integrations.
Implement secure authentication via Managed Identity (Entra ID) — no secrets in code; reusable across other agents.
Implement single-incident-per-conversation continuity — conversation_id → correlation_id, one conversation maps to exactly one incident.
Prepare integration interfaces/placeholders for the client ticketing APIs — agent tool layer stubbed until live ServiceNow APIs/credentials arrive.
Create the Ticket (Interaction/IMS) and Incident (INC) data models/response templates — the exact fields the orchestrator consumes.
Implement testing with dummy data until actual APIs are available — agent-generated placeholder IDs + Postman end-to-end flow.
